---
// Terms of use for kinderform.org. English law. Keep in step with /privacy and /licences.
import Legal from "@/layouts/Legal.astro";

const h2 = "scroll-m-20 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight";
const p = "leading-7";
const ul = "ml-5 list-disc space-y-2 leading-7";
const link = "font-medium underline underline-offset-4";
const email = "jamie@kinderform.org";
---
<Legal
  title="Terms of use: Kinderform"
  heading="Terms of use"
  description="The rules for using kinderform.org, its starter kits, data and research. Kinderform is free, is not a fostering or adoption service and gives no professional advice."
  current="/terms"
  updated="28 November 2026"
>
  <div slot="summary" class="space-y-4">
    <p class="text-xl leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
      Kinderform is free to use. These terms explain what it is, what it is not, and who is responsible for what.
    </p>
    <div class="rounded-lg border p-4">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold">The short version</h2>
      <ul class={`${ul} mt-2`}>
        <li>Kinderform is not a fostering or adoption service. It does not pass on enquiries.</li>
        <li>Nothing here is legal, social work or other professional advice.</li>
        <li>Facts can be wrong or out of date. Check the source and date before you rely on one.</li>
        <li>If your service uses our kits, you are responsible for your own form and the data it collects.</li>
        <li>You can reuse our code, writing and data under open licences. Some things are not open.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section aria-labelledby="who" class="space-y-4">
    <h2 id="who" class={h2}>1. Who runs Kinderform</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      Kinderform (kinderform.org) is a free, non-commercial project run by Jamie Gannaway, a private individual who
      lives in Barcelona, Spain. It is not a company, a charity or a government body.
    </p>
    <p class={p}>
      In these terms, "we" and "us" mean Jamie. "You" means anyone who uses the site, its downloads or its repository
      on GitHub.
    </p>
    <p class={p}>
      Contact: <a href={`mailto:${email}`} class={link}>{email}</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="agree" class="space-y-4">
    <h2 id="agree" class={h2}>2. Agreeing to these terms</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      By using Kinderform, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please do not use it.
    </p>
    <p class={p}>
      If you use Kinderform for an organisation, you confirm you may accept these terms for it. "You" then includes
      that organisation.
    </p>
    <p class={p}>
      These terms, the <a href="/privacy" class={link}>privacy policy</a> and the
      <a href="/licences" class={link}>licences</a> are the whole agreement between you and us about Kinderform.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="what" class="space-y-4">
    <h2 id="what" class={h2}>3. What Kinderform is, and what it is not</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      Kinderform offers research, data, draft standards, example forms and starter kits. They help fostering and
      adoption services give a kinder first reply to people who enquire.
    </p>
    <ul class={ul}>
      <li>
        <strong>It is not a fostering or adoption service.</strong> It does not take, judge or pass on enquiries. The
        example forms send nothing.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>It is not linked to any government.</strong> The example forms use public design systems, but no
        government made, approved or supports Kinderform.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>It is not endorsed by the services it describes.</strong> Naming a service does not mean it agrees with
        or supports Kinderform.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>It gives no professional advice.</strong> Nothing here is legal, social work, data protection, medical
        or other professional advice. Get your own advice before acting.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class={p}>
      If you want to foster or adopt, contact a service directly.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="accuracy" class="space-y-4">
    <h2 id="accuracy" class={h2}>4. Information can be wrong or out of date</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      We build our research with AI tools and check it by hand. That checking is not finished. Each page says what a
      person has checked and when.
    </p>
    <p class={p}>
      Services change their pages and rules often. Our tables describe public pages on the date we read them.
    </p>
    <p class={p}>
      Check the original source and date before you rely on a fact or quote it. The standard, the checklist and the
      kits are drafts and may change.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="kits" class="space-y-4">
    <h2 id="kits" class={h2}>5. Using the starter kits, schema and AI prompt in your service</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      You may use them to build or improve your own enquiry form. If you do, your organisation is responsible for:
    </p>
    <ul class={ul}>
      <li>the form, its wording and the replies it sends</li>
      <li>following the law where you work, including data protection, equality and accessibility law</li>
      <li>the personal information your form collects, as its controller, with your own privacy notice</li>
      <li>checking anything an AI tool writes for you before you use it</li>
      <li>testing the form with made-up details before real people use it</li>
    </ul>
    <p class={p}>
      Kinderform never receives or handles the information people put into your form. We are not your data processor.
    </p>
    <p class={p}>
      Never put real personal information into an example form, a test record or the GitHub repository.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="licences" class="space-y-4">
    <h2 id="licences" class={h2}>6. Reusing our work</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      Our code is under the MIT licence. Our writing and data are under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (CC BY 4.0).
      You can reuse them for any purpose, including commercial use, if you follow the licence.
    </p>
    <p class={p}>
      Some things are not open, including the drawings, Jamie's photograph and the Kinderform name. The
      <a href="/licences" class={link}>licences page</a> lists what you can and cannot reuse.
    </p>
    <p class={p}>
      If a licence and these terms disagree about reusing material, the licence wins.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="name" class="space-y-4">
    <h2 id="name" class={h2}>7. The Kinderform name</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      The open licences do not cover the Kinderform name or logo. You may use the name to credit us, or to say your work
      is based on Kinderform.
    </p>
    <p class={p}>
      Do not use the name or logo to suggest we made, approved or support your form, product or service. The exception
      is when we agree in writing.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="contribute" class="space-y-4">
    <h2 id="contribute" class={h2}>8. Contributing</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      When you send code, writing, data or corrections to Kinderform, you agree that:
    </p>
    <ul class={ul}>
      <li>code you send is licensed under the MIT licence, and anything else under CC BY 4.0</li>
      <li>you have the right to give it under those licences</li>
      <li>it holds no real personal information and copies no licensed form</li>
      <li>we may edit it, use it, credit you for it, or decide not to use it</li>
    </ul>
    <p class={p}>
      Ideas and feedback you send are free for us to use. We will only quote you, even without your name, if you say we
      may.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="use" class="space-y-4">
    <h2 id="use" class={h2}>9. Things you must not do</h2>
    <ul class={ul}>
      <li>break the law, or help someone else break it</li>
      <li>try to get round the site's security, or harm, overload or disrupt it</li>
      <li>upload viruses or other harmful code</li>
      <li>send or post real personal information about anyone else, especially a child</li>
      <li>pretend to be a service, a government body or someone else</li>
      <li>harass, threaten or abuse anyone, including service staff</li>
      <li>use Kinderform to score, rank or screen people who offer to care, or to treat them unfairly</li>
    </ul>
    <p class={p}>
      Our GitHub repository and WhatsApp community also follow our
      <a href="https://github.com/jamiegannaway/kinderform/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md" class={link}>code of conduct</a>.
      We may remove posts or people who break these rules.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="reply" class="space-y-4">
    <h2 id="reply" class={h2}>10. Corrections and the right of reply</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      If something about your service is wrong, tell us. Give the public page, what changed and the date you checked.
    </p>
    <p class={p}>
      We look at every correction and tell you what we did. Before we publish a score for a named service, that service
      can see it privately and reply.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="links" class="space-y-4">
    <h2 id="links" class={h2}>11. Other websites</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      We link to services, research and other sites. We do not control them and are not responsible for what they say
      or do.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="change" class="space-y-4">
    <h2 id="change" class={h2}>12. We may change or stop Kinderform</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      Kinderform is free and run by one person. We may change, pause or stop any part of it at any time, without
      notice.
    </p>
    <p class={p}>
      We cannot promise the site will always be available or free of errors. Downloads you already have stay under
      their licences.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="liability" class="space-y-4">
    <h2 id="liability" class={h2}>13. Our responsibility to you</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      We provide Kinderform free and "as is". As far as the law allows, we give no promises about it beyond those in
      these terms.
    </p>
    <p class={p}>
      As far as the law allows, we are not responsible for any loss caused by using or relying on Kinderform. The same
      applies if you cannot use it.
    </p>
    <p class={p}>
      If you use Kinderform for an organisation, we are not responsible for lost profit, revenue, data, contracts or
      goodwill. We are also not responsible for any indirect loss.
    </p>
    <p class={p}>
      If we are found responsible to an organisation in any case, our total responsibility is limited to £100.
    </p>
    <p class={p}>
      <strong>Some responsibility cannot be limited.</strong> Nothing in these terms limits our responsibility for
      death or personal injury caused by our negligence, or for fraud. It also does not limit anything else the law
      does not allow us to limit.
    </p>
    <p class={p}>
      If you use Kinderform as a private person, you keep all the rights the law gives you that cannot be removed by
      agreement.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="law" class="space-y-4">
    <h2 id="law" class={h2}>14. Which law applies</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      The law of England and Wales applies to these terms and to any dispute about Kinderform. The courts of England
      and Wales can decide disputes.
    </p>
    <p class={p}>
      If you are a private person, you keep the protection of the law where you live. You can also bring a claim in the
      courts where you live.
    </p>
    <p class={p}>
      Please talk to us first. Most problems can be fixed with an email.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="general" class="space-y-4">
    <h2 id="general" class={h2}>15. Other legal points</h2>
    <ul class={ul}>
      <li>If a court decides part of these terms cannot be enforced, the rest still applies.</li>
      <li>If we do not enforce a term straight away, we can still enforce it later.</li>
      <li>Only you and we can enforce these terms. Nobody else has rights under them.</li>
      <li>You may not pass your rights under these terms to anyone else.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="updates" class="space-y-4">
    <h2 id="updates" class={h2}>16. Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      We may update these terms. We will change the date at the top, and every past version stays public on GitHub.
    </p>
    <p class={p}>
      If you keep using Kinderform after a change, the new terms apply to you from then on.
    </p>
  </section>
</Legal>
